WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.739 --> 00:00:15.220
Outside in the cool night, Romeo paused in a lane beside the wall of the Capulets' garden.

2
00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:18.161
"How can I go forward when my heart is back there?"

3
00:00:18.221 --> 00:00:18.641
he thought.

4
00:00:19.301 --> 00:00:23.543
He heard his friends calling for him as they left the dance, and somehow their laughter and clowning

5
00:00:23.923 --> 00:00:25.103
helped him make up his mind.

6
00:00:25.503 --> 00:00:27.624
He climbed the wall and leapt down on the other side.

7
00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:32.583
The garden was small, and above it a balcony extended from a second-floor bedroom.

8
00:00:33.284 --> 00:00:34.505
A light came on in the window.

9
00:00:34.525 --> 00:00:35.966
"What light is this?"

10
00:00:36.247 --> 00:00:38.428
he asked softly and quickly hid in the shadows.

11
00:00:39.109 --> 00:00:43.753
His heart leapt when he saw Juliet step out into the night, and with a smile to himself

12
00:00:43.793 --> 00:00:47.996
he answered his own question: "This light is the East, and Juliet is the sun!"

13
00:00:49.598 --> 00:00:52.820
Juliet leaned on the balcony rail, with her cheek resting on her hand.

14
00:00:53.361 --> 00:00:54.922
Deep in thought, she sighed his name.

15
00:00:54.942 --> 00:00:59.142
"Oh Romeo," she said, not seeing him below.

16
00:00:59.162 --> 00:01:01.644
"Why do you have to be named ‘Romeo'?

17
00:01:02.264 --> 00:01:04.606
A rose, by any other name, would smell as sweet.

18
00:01:05.287 --> 00:01:09.430
But if you won't deny your name, just swear you'll love me and I'll marry you and no

19
00:01:09.470 --> 00:01:10.551
longer be a Capulet."

20
00:01:11.391 --> 00:01:15.555
"My dear saint, I take you at your word," Romeo called out happily from below.

21
00:01:16.656 --> 00:01:20.379
Juliet knew who it was as soon as she heard his voice and looked down with joy to

22
00:01:20.419 --> 00:01:21.620
see Romeo standing there.

23
00:01:22.360 --> 00:01:24.662
She blushed and wished that she could recall her words.

24
00:01:24.682 --> 00:01:26.484
"Do you love me, in truth?"

25
00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:27.721
she asked.

26
00:01:28.261 --> 00:01:30.763
"I have given you my heart's answer before you even asked."

27
00:01:32.184 --> 00:01:35.868
"My love for you is as deep and boundless as the sea," Romeo replied.

28
00:01:36.548 --> 00:01:40.151
With this exchange, Romeo and Juliet promised their love to each other.

29
00:01:40.772 --> 00:01:46.537
Despite the danger that Romeo might be discovered by Juliet's kinsmen, they couldn't tear themselves away from each

30
00:01:46.597 --> 00:01:48.859
other and continued whispering under the moon.

31
00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:54.384
They both feared that this new love, so sudden and bright as lightning, might disappear as quickly.

32
00:01:55.124 --> 00:01:59.186
So they were already talking of marriage when Juliet's nurse called for her from the bedroom.

33
00:02:00.027 --> 00:02:04.309
"Tomorrow, I'll send you word about where and when we can be married," Romeo whispered urgently.

34
00:02:04.330 --> 00:02:10.533
"I'm coming," Juliet called back to her nurse, and then to Romeo she said, "Parting is such sweet

35
00:02:10.613 --> 00:02:13.575
sorrow, but now I must say goodnight."

36
00:02:14.335 --> 00:02:18.738
When she had disappeared from the balcony, Romeo leapt over the garden wall as lightly as if love

37
00:02:18.778 --> 00:02:19.699
had given him wings.

38
00:02:20.939 --> 00:02:25.097
Too excited to sleep, he hurried to a nearby monastery to find Friar Lawrence.

39
00:02:25.858 --> 00:02:29.799
The friendly monk was performing his early morning devotions when Romeo interrupted him.

40
00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:35.702
In a gush, Romeo explained everything, how he and Juliet had met and fallen in love.

41
00:02:36.642 --> 00:02:39.483
He asked the friar to marry them in secret that very afternoon.

42
00:02:40.284 --> 00:02:42.365
Friar Lawrence thought Romeo was being rash.

43
00:02:42.385 --> 00:02:44.465
"Be wise and slow.

44
00:02:45.106 --> 00:02:50.108
They stumble who run too fast," said the friar, but in the end he agreed to Romeo's request.

45
00:02:51.168 --> 00:02:54.571
He had always been fond of Romeo and believed that his love was sincere.

46
00:02:55.692 --> 00:03:00.896
Secretly, he hoped that this young love between a Montague and a Capulet might begin to heal the

47
00:03:00.956 --> 00:03:02.537
hatred between the two houses.

48
00:03:03.638 --> 00:03:06.920
Romeo was in high spirits as he returned from the monastery.

49
00:03:08.121 --> 00:03:12.645
He met Mercutio and Benvolio in the street, who were curious about where he had gone after the

50
00:03:12.685 --> 00:03:16.788
dance. He traded jokes with them, but cleverly avoided answering their questions.

51
00:03:17.516 --> 00:03:22.059
When Juliet's nurse approached, he said good-bye to his friends, promising to dine with them later.

52
00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:27.143
Quickly he explained to the nurse the arrangements he had made with the friar, and she left to

53
00:03:27.183 --> 00:03:28.364
give the news to Juliet.

54
00:03:29.024 --> 00:03:33.447
Juliet, who had been too excited to sleep all night, was waiting impatiently in her father's garden.

55
00:03:34.027 --> 00:03:36.969
When her nurse arrived, she quickly burst out, "Did you see him?

56
00:03:37.210 --> 00:03:37.930
What did he say?"

57
00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:40.232
"Have patience, just a minute!

58
00:03:40.652 --> 00:03:44.475
Oh, how my bones ache," said the nurse with a sour face.

59
00:03:44.495 --> 00:03:46.256
"I am so out of breath.

60
00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:50.161
All this running back and forth through the town is enough to give me a backache.

61
00:03:51.181 --> 00:03:53.402
You certainly know how to put your nurse to the test.

62
00:03:54.702 --> 00:03:56.943
I've never been asked to do such a journey so quickly.

63
00:03:57.643 --> 00:04:01.104
Even your mother, when she sends me to the market "My mother?

64
00:04:01.324 --> 00:04:04.545
I didn't ask you about my mother," said Juliet impatiently.

65
00:04:04.565 --> 00:04:06.445
"What did Romeo say?"

66
00:04:06.465 --> 00:04:09.586
"The young are so impatient," said the nurse.

67
00:04:10.286 --> 00:04:14.828
And then before Juliet could pester her with more questions, she asked, "Do you have time to go

68
00:04:14.868 --> 00:04:15.668
to church today?"

69
00:04:16.656 --> 00:04:17.777
"I have," said Juliet.

70
00:04:17.797 --> 00:04:19.519
"Well hurry then.

71
00:04:19.619 --> 00:04:24.544
Because this afternoon, at Friar Lawrence's monastery, you'll find a husband waiting to make you his wife!"

72
00:04:24.564 --> 00:04:26.826
"Oh thank you, Nurse!"

73
00:04:27.346 --> 00:04:28.567
said Juliet and hugged her.

74
00:04:28.928 --> 00:04:31.270
Then the nurse told her everything Romeo had said.

75
00:04:32.231 --> 00:04:36.775
When Juliet arrived at the church, Romeo was indeed waiting for her there with Friar Lawrence.

76
00:04:38.136 --> 00:04:42.060
They were so happy to see each other that the friar couldn't help but smile too.

77
00:04:43.048 --> 00:04:48.111
"If the richest man counted all his wealth, he would be a beggar compared to this uncountable happiness,"

78
00:04:48.151 --> 00:04:48.572
he said.

79
00:04:48.592 --> 00:04:52.314
"Come, join hands, and I will join your souls in marriage."

80
00:04:53.095 --> 00:04:58.818
When the ceremony ended and the friar had prayed, "Heaven smile on this holy act," the young couple

81
00:04:58.878 --> 00:05:00.239
reluctantly said goodbye.

82
00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:05.623
They promised to meet again that night and planned where to place a ladder so that Romeo could

83
00:05:05.663 --> 00:05:07.624
climb up to the balcony to be with Juliet.

84
00:05:08.928 --> 00:05:13.209
That same afternoon, Tybalt was leading a group of Capulets through the city looking for Romeo.

85
00:05:13.969 --> 00:05:19.851
When he came across Benvolio and Mercutio in the city square, he insolently demanded to know where Romeo

86
00:05:19.891 --> 00:05:22.812
was. Romeo's friends quickly took offense.

87
00:05:23.532 --> 00:05:26.353
Tybalt, they could see, was planning some violence against Romeo.

88
00:05:27.993 --> 00:05:33.375
Mercutio pulled his sword, then Tybalt drew his sword, and while they were still arguing, Romeo entered the

89
00:05:33.415 --> 00:05:37.436
square. "Aha," cried Tybalt, "here comes the villain!

90
00:05:37.972 --> 00:05:40.033
Romeo, stand and put up your sword."

91
00:05:40.754 --> 00:05:46.477
Romeo, you must remember, was just returning from his wedding, so the old feud was the furthest thing

92
00:05:46.517 --> 00:05:47.257
from his mind.

93
00:05:47.277 --> 00:05:50.979
"I am no villain of yours, Tybalt," Romeo protested calmly.

94
00:05:50.999 --> 00:05:54.481
"In fact, I love the name Capulet as dearly as my own."

95
00:05:55.261 --> 00:06:00.724
Mercutio was neither a Capulet nor a Montague, but he was one of Romeo's oldest friends, and he

96
00:06:00.784 --> 00:06:03.306
was as impetuous and headstrong as Tybalt.

97
00:06:04.026 --> 00:06:07.748
Pushing Romeo aside, he faced Tybalt and called him a hateful, stinking dog.

98
00:06:08.320 --> 00:06:11.242
Tybalt answered with a swing of his sword, and they began to fight.

99
00:06:12.043 --> 00:06:14.384
"Stop this outrage," cried Romeo.

100
00:06:15.785 --> 00:06:17.366
"Fools, the prince will arrest you!"

101
00:06:17.687 --> 00:06:22.570
cried Benvolio, and together, he and Romeo rushed in to separate the two fighters.

102
00:06:23.230 --> 00:06:29.335
Romeo took hold of Mercutio's arm, but before Benvolio could restrain Tybalt, the young Capulet struck Mercutio with

103
00:06:29.415 --> 00:06:30.495
a thrust through the chest.

104
00:06:31.256 --> 00:06:36.840
Mercutio cried out in pain, and, seeing him collapse in Romeo's arms, Tybalt quickly turned to escape.

105
00:06:37.588 --> 00:06:40.309
Romeo could see in his friend's eyes that he was fatally wounded.

106
00:06:41.129 --> 00:06:43.150
Mercutio, too, knew he was dying.

107
00:06:43.170 --> 00:06:45.850
"A plague on both your houses!"

108
00:06:46.351 --> 00:06:46.951
he gasped.

109
00:06:47.391 --> 00:06:48.231
"I am slain."

110
00:06:49.311 --> 00:06:51.052
Romeo could not contain his rage.

111
00:06:51.732 --> 00:06:54.473
He laid Mercutio on the pavement and pulled his sword.

112
00:06:54.493 --> 00:06:56.273
"Stay, Tybalt!"

113
00:06:56.654 --> 00:06:58.314
he called out in a furious challenge.

114
00:06:59.054 --> 00:07:04.816
"Stay to keep my dead companion company, because, God help me, you will accompany him to the grave!"
